From 72e169b1ed5f12dfa8272e0886ce9753cf4a1b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:46:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: keep the multiplier-kill timer when checking whether to
 rest

borg_check_rest() refuses to rest for a few turns after the Borg killed
a multiplying monster, so it does not sit down next to unseen breeders.
It also cleared the timer as soon as the check got past that test, which
is the case on the turn of the kill itself (the test needs the timer to
be above zero). The next check, one turn later, found no recent kill and
allowed resting. Do not clear the timer.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#149.

(cherry picked from commit e66740cc4563224ca5dddab5d7bd543d8c8f1342)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c
index 81c526a36..5b0957e69 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-misc.c
@@ -1243,9 +1243,6 @@ bool borg_check_rest(int y, int x)
         && (borg.trait[BI_CURSP] >= borg.trait[BI_MAXSP] * 7 / 10))
         return false;
 
-    /* Set this to Zero */
-    borg.time.last_kill_mult = 0;
-
     /* Most of the time, its ok to rest in a vault */
     if (borg.status.vault) {
         for (i = -1; i < 1; i++) {
-- 
2.53.0

